    "aqua": {
      "word": "AQUA",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "Water; -- a word much used in pharmacy and the old chemistry, in various signification, determined by the word or words annexed. Aqua ammoniæ, the aqueous solution of ammonia; liquid ammonia; often called aqua ammonia. fuming yellow liquid consisting of nitric and hydrochloric acids. It has the power of dissolving gold, the \"royal\" metal. poisoning, made by an Italian woman named Tofana, in the middle of the 17th century, who is said to have poisoned more than 600 persons. Francis. a name given to brandy and some other ardent spirits. Shak.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        }
      ],
      "relatedWords": []
    },
